{
  "dom_id": "question-133298",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Fred purchased his land for $200$ thousand dollars. The value of the land increases by $10%$ each year. How much will Fred's plot be worth after $4$ years? Round your answer to the nearest thousand dollars.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        After $4$ years, the land will be worth approximately \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n thousand dollars.",
  "worked_solution": "The land initially costs $200$ thousand, which increases at a rate of $10%$ per year.\n\n$10%$ as a decimal is $0.1.$ Therefore, an increase of $10%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.1=1.1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value will be $200\\cdot (1.1)$ thousand dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value will be $200\\cdot (1.1)^{2}$ thousand dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value will be $200\\cdot (1.1)^{3}$ thousand dollars.\n\n- After $4$ years, the value will be $200\\cdot (1.1)^{4}$ thousand dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the value after $4$ years, we get the following:\n\n$$\n200\\cdot (1.1)^{4}=292.82≈293,\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, after $4$ years, the land will be worth approximately $293$ thousand dollars.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
